WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:06.090
Ever since we took those first steps out of
the primordial soup, mankind has long since

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:10.930
looked to the night sky and dreamed of setting
out among the stars.

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:18.640
Space is, as it has been said, the final frontier;
that vast, inky void that, for all its perils,

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:24.130
still holds a sense of wonder and calls us
to venture out and explore the cosmos.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:28.419
The earliest missions of the Space Race during
the fifties and sixties showed the people

00:00:28.419 --> 00:00:34.300
of Earth that, while it wasn’t easy, the
dream of achieving space travel was possible.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:39.550
And that dream, the willingness to chase it,
is all you really need to get there.

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:44.100
Well, that, plus a couple of friends and a
Volkswagen microbus.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:48.480
For William, that dream of traveling away
from Earth and up to the starry skies was

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:49.950
inescapable.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:53.930
At twenty-one, he was a guy like many others
growing up in the fifties.

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:58.690
His friends and family all thought of him
as a bit of a beatnik, who was in deep with

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:01.260
a lot of hip counter-culture types.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:06.830
William had even dabbled in a few alternative
religious groups as well, most notably practices

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:12.970
like the action of Transcendental Meditation,
as well as the teachings of Meher Baba, an

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:17.110
Indian spiritual leader who claimed to be
God in human form.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:21.590
In other words, William would have been a
full-blown hippy in the sixties, if he’d

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:24.520
only lived long enough to see them.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:29.220
Even now, the idea of taking a summer road
trip with a small group of close friends isn’t

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:30.220
unheard of.

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:34.730
And that’s almost exactly what William had
in mind during the summer of 1958, but with

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:38.030
a few key differences.

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:43.780
For one, this was set to be a one-way road
trip, with zero plans for a return journey.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:44.880
And why?

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:50.150
You guessed it: It was because William and
his pals wanted to go to outer space.

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:56.180
More specifically, they wanted to drive to
space, to leave the world behind and cruise

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:59.540
all the way out into the shining lights of
the solar system.

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:05.370
In March, William bought a brand-new microbus,
a Volkswagen Type 2 Samba-Bus after pooling

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:11.000
money for a down payment with his three friends,
Jerry, Sam, and Susan.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:15.420
Ask anyone nowadays to picture an old-school
minivan, and they’d probably end up describing

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.870
the exact same type of bus.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:21.500
What had spurred them to buy a bus in the
hopes of traveling off-world in it?

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:26.940
Well, the three had recently been excommunicated
from the Fifth Church, a highly secretive

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:28.780
new age religion.

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:33.370
Members of the Church, or “Fifthists”,
are all about conformity and control - you

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:39.560
may remember these eccentric folks from our
video on SCP-3512 - The More You Know - but

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:43.620
William’s intention of traveling to space
seemed to conflict with the Fifth Church’s

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:48.130
beliefs, most likely on account of his free
spirit defying a group whose two main hobbies

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:51.500
were obsessing over patterns and mind control.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:55.850
The young man believed there was magic up
there among the stars, and refused to work

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:59.819
a boring nine to five waiting for that magic
to come down to Earth.

00:02:59.819 --> 00:03:04.510
So, with the help of Jerry, he began to work
on modifying the bus.

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:10.130
Heaven was up there, and according to William,
it was waiting for its angels.

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:13.370
It took about two months, but Jerry came through.

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:17.780
The engine compartment and cabin of the microbus
were now air-tight, with the section near

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:20.420
the rear doors transformed into an airlock.

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:25.290
The windows were replaced with shatterproof
acrylic, the outer surface treated to withstand

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:26.990
any space debris.

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:31.880
The gas tank had been replaced with technology
decades ahead of its time, but the steering

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:37.250
wheel, gear shift, hand brake, and pedals
all functioned exactly the same.

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:41.740
One look at the outer panels of the microbus
would have told you what it was, and where

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:42.740
it was heading.

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:48.209
The word “Starmobile” was spray-painted
on one side and on the other “Alpha Centauri

00:03:48.209 --> 00:03:49.410
or bust”.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:53.340
The fourth of July rolled around and their
Starmobile took flight.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:57.489
William, keeping a diary of their journey,
referred to himself and his friends as the

00:03:57.489 --> 00:04:01.490
only four people in the universe who were
truly free.

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:06.140
Careening upwards at eighty-two miles per
hour, without any police to stop them, no

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:12.739
longer restricted by mundane life on Earth,
the group traveled higher in their microbus.

00:04:12.739 --> 00:04:18.019
Their plan was to travel straight to Alpha
Centauri, the closest star and planetary system

00:04:18.019 --> 00:04:20.299
to our own solar system.

00:04:20.299 --> 00:04:25.020
Thinking their journey would only last a few
short weeks, William and his friends waved

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:26.710
farewell to Earth.

00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:31.870
The bus had everything on board that these
intergalactic travelers could possibly need,

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:36.490
from bedrolls and pillows to sleep on, to
enough dehydrated food to feed the four of

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:39.300
them for three whole months in space.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:44.210
There was even room aboard the microbus for
Susan’s cat Milly, as well as all the comforts

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:45.280
of home.

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:49.400
William and his friends packed bongos, a guitar
and countless books.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:54.639
But this road trip wasn’t just an aimless
joyride out into the cosmos.

00:04:54.639 --> 00:04:59.879
The intrepid group had enough supplies with
them, and enough ambition, to set up the first

00:04:59.879 --> 00:05:01.259
off-world human colony.

00:05:01.259 --> 00:05:06.550
They’d packed a seed bank, containing hundreds,
if not thousands, of varying seeds from a

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:09.360
number of common domestic plants from Earth.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:14.479
On top of that, there were even frozen egg
cells of domestic animals like cats and dogs

00:05:14.479 --> 00:05:17.710
and livestock such as cows and pigs.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:22.300
These embryos were all ready to be unfrozen
and allowed to grow once the gang reached

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:23.300
their destination.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:27.100
However, it didn’t take long for problems
to start arising.

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:32.620
For one, the group quickly ran out of libations
within the first five days of leaving Earth.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:38.460
Spirits were naturally dampened by the absence
of spirits, but William tried to remain optimistic,

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:42.939
hoping to grow barley and concoct some homemade
brew once they arrived at Alpha Centauri.

00:05:42.939 --> 00:05:49.729
But, while the lack of ale and lager was an
inconvenience, there was worse on the horizon.

00:05:49.729 --> 00:05:53.529
During a group sing-along, something collided
with the Starmobile.

00:05:53.529 --> 00:05:58.569
Naturally, all aboard were rattled, and it
was Jerry who stepped up to calm everyone,

00:05:58.569 --> 00:06:01.999
stating it was likely just space dust or debris.

00:06:01.999 --> 00:06:06.900
He opted to take a look outside and see if
there had been any damage to the microbus.

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:11.759
Donning a homemade space suit, Jerry left
via the airlock at the rear of the bus and

00:06:11.759 --> 00:06:14.509
examined, finding that no significant harm
had been done.

00:06:14.509 --> 00:06:19.600
But as he was about to make his way back inside,
something struck the Starmobile again.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:25.229
The force of it caused Jerry to lose his grip,
sending him drifting out into space.

00:06:25.229 --> 00:06:29.419
William was the only one at the wheel of the
bus but had never learned to drive.

00:06:29.419 --> 00:06:34.479
Eventually, he was able to turn the Samba-Bus
around, but it was too late.

00:06:34.479 --> 00:06:38.339
Jerry was dead, adrift in the cold vacuum.

00:06:38.339 --> 00:06:42.219
The loss overwhelmed the group but hit Susan
worst of all.

00:06:42.219 --> 00:06:46.800
She and Jerry had wanted to get married the
moment that they arrived at Alpha Centauri.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:50.999
William had even obtained a minister’s license
so he could officiate his friends’ wedding

00:06:50.999 --> 00:06:53.180
that would now never happen.

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:57.539
Three days later, Sam and William awoke to
find Susan dead on the floor of the bus.

00:06:57.539 --> 00:07:00.710
The grief and sorrow had gotten too much for
her.

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:04.289
According to William’s diary, she died of
a broken heart.

00:07:04.289 --> 00:07:08.960
Drawing up his guitar and strumming Amazing
Grace for his second dead friend, William

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:12.689
watched as Sam let Susan’s body drift out
of the airlock.

00:07:12.689 --> 00:07:17.599
He wrote in his journal that he hoped she
would find Jerry out there in space, at least

00:07:17.599 --> 00:07:19.279
they would be together.

00:07:19.279 --> 00:07:24.280
By now, it had been well over fifty days since
the Starmobile had left the safe confines

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:25.749
of Planet Earth.

00:07:25.749 --> 00:07:31.569
The group had suffered two tragic, heartbreaking
casualties already, one by accident and one

00:07:31.569 --> 00:07:33.039
as a result of the first.

00:07:33.039 --> 00:07:38.460
And yet, William and Sam, the survivors, were
still traveling ever deeper into the dark

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:43.770
void above, plotting their course to Alpha
Centauri as best they could with the hand-drawn

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:46.219
star charts that they had brought with them.

00:07:46.219 --> 00:07:51.279
So far, their journey into space had begun
with promise and optimism and was now fraught

00:07:51.279 --> 00:07:53.740
with dangers and obstacles.

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:56.059
And these were far from over.

00:07:56.059 --> 00:08:00.439
Slowly, William began to realize that it was
taking much longer to reach their destination

00:08:00.439 --> 00:08:03.059
than he and Jerry had first anticipated.

00:08:03.059 --> 00:08:07.389
Alpha Centauri is roughly four and a half
light-years from Earth, bear in mind that

00:08:07.389 --> 00:08:11.349
a single light-year is equivalent to roughly
six trillion miles.

00:08:11.349 --> 00:08:15.610
William was unsure if the microbus had been
traveling in the wrong direction, or if it

00:08:15.610 --> 00:08:18.800
had even managed to miss the terminus of the
journey.

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:23.490
The charts Jerry had drawn were of little
help, he had been the expert, the one who

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:28.740
planned the trip and modified the Volkswagen
Type 2 Samba-Bus for space travel.

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:33.680
William was out of his depth, hurtling through
the galaxy with little help from his passenger.

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:38.470
To make matters worse, both William and Sam
had started feeling unwell.

00:08:38.470 --> 00:08:43.209
Not just travel sick, as you might expect
after spending a long ride in a microbus trundling

00:08:43.209 --> 00:08:44.500
through space.

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:48.209
Their illness wasn’t even caused by being
trapped in the cramped space for such a long

00:08:48.209 --> 00:08:49.740
duration of time.

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:55.290
Blotches had begun to appear all over their
skin, and Sam had been having trouble eating.

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:59.459
At random, even a tooth spontaneously fell
out of his mouth.

00:08:59.459 --> 00:09:02.589
These aren’t symptoms typical of space travel
though.

00:09:02.589 --> 00:09:08.160
Due to a severe lack of Vitamin C in the food
they had packed, the pair of them had developed

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:09.160
scurvy.

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:13.519
Just as it seemed like the trip to Alpha Centauri
couldn’t have been a bigger disaster, William

00:09:13.519 --> 00:09:16.920
awoke to see something out of the microbus
window.

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:21.550
Something he had probably seen hundreds of
times in his lifetime, but seeing it now filled

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:22.670
him with dread.

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:26.779
It was the Moon, as in Earth’s Moon.

00:09:26.779 --> 00:09:30.220
They were barely close to Alpha Centauri.

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:33.980
Quickly realizing that they would never reach
their destination on their current course

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:39.329
due to their grievous errors in calculation,
William did the only thing he could.

00:09:39.329 --> 00:09:44.730
He closed the curtains so that Sam couldn’t
see how big of a mistake they had made.

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:47.870
Eventually, Milly crawled behind the sofa
and died.

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:50.980
Meanwhile, Sam stopped being able to keep
his food down.

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:54.940
Towards the end, he could barely so much as
see or even sit.

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:58.990
Every time he asked his friend if they had
arrived yet, William would tell him that they

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:00.649
would be there tomorrow.

00:10:00.649 --> 00:10:03.720
He couldn’t bring himself to tell Sam the
truth.

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:10.000
Finally, Sam asked William to read to him,
a poem by Dylan Thomas called And Death Shall

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.209
Have No Dominion.

00:10:11.209 --> 00:10:14.920
He was dead before William finished reading.

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:18.750
Saddened and filled with remorse, William
pushed the last of his friends out of the

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:24.589
airlock, realizing that no one would be left
to push him out when he eventually died.

00:10:24.589 --> 00:10:28.579
The final thought he recorded in his diary
came after another two whole months spent

00:10:28.579 --> 00:10:32.290
isolated and alone in space before William’s
death.

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:37.120
The last thing he wrote was that the stars
looked so beautiful against the dark backdrop

00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:38.579
of the universe.

00:10:38.579 --> 00:10:44.750
In spite of the tragedy of his situation,
so few others - especially from his time - would

00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:47.100
ever truly see them like this.

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:50.920
Today, the bus is still drifting quietly through
space.

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:57.680
Now known as SCP-1958, it rests in orbit of
Mars, the withered remains of its driver still

00:10:57.680 --> 00:10:59.459
sitting at the wheel.

00:10:59.459 --> 00:11:04.399
William and his friends never made it to Alpha
Centauri, in fact, it would have taken them

00:11:04.399 --> 00:11:07.319
almost forty million years to reach it.

00:11:07.319 --> 00:11:11.839
They never saw their dream come to the ending
that they had planned.

00:11:11.839 --> 00:11:19.420
Instead, William, Jerry, Sam, Susan, and Milly
the cat all died among the stars, driving

00:11:19.420 --> 00:11:24.449
their magic bus, their Starmobile out into
the unknown.

00:11:24.449 --> 00:11:30.720
For them, space, that final frontier, had
a lot more finality to it.

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:38.450
Now go check out “How NOT to Kill an SCP
- SCP-1609 - Remains of a Chair” and “SCP-701

00:11:38.450 --> 00:11:42.779
- The Hanged King's Tragedy” for more anomalies
that veer into the tragic!

